 "note_en": "The function word 被 forms the passive: first the one something happens to, then 被, then (optionally) who does it, then the verb. 您的账户会被冻结 \"your account will be frozen\" — who freezes it isn't said. In 从来没被人怀疑过 the doer is named — 人, \"anyone\": \"he had never been suspected by anyone.\" The negative 没 goes before 被, not before the verb.",
